@startuml interservice-security
title Lakehouse - service-to-service security

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #444444
    ActorBorderColor #2C5D8A
    LifeCycleBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBorderColor #2C5D8A
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F0F8
}

participant "Caller service\n(config-svc / state-svc /\ntask-executor-svc /\nscheduler-svc / task-proxy)" as Caller
participant "Keycloak\n(realm: lakehouse)" as KC
participant "Resource service\n(backend REST API)" as RS

== Background processing (Kafka consumer, scheduler, task processor) ==

note over Caller
    No user JWT in SecurityContextHolder
    -> fallback to client_credentials
end note

Caller -> KC : POST /protocol/openid-connect/token\ngrant_type=client_credentials\nclient_id=lakehouse-internal-client
KC --> Caller : access_token (JWT, cached by\nOAuth2AuthorizedClientManager)

Caller -> RS : REST request\nAuthorization: Bearer <service-account JWT>

== Request handled by the resource server ==

note over RS #FFF3D6
    Whitelist (no auth): /healthz, /readyz,
    /actuator/**, /v3/api-docs/**, /swagger-ui/**
end note

RS -> RS : Validate JWT signature (issuer-uri / JWKS)
RS -> RS : KeycloakRoleConverter:\nrealm_access.roles -> ROLE_<NAME>
RS -> RS : AuditLoggingFilter -> AUDIT_LOG (JSON):\nUser ID, Username ("system" for service accounts),\nMethod, URI, HTTP status
RS --> Caller : 200 OK

== User-initiated processing (token relay) ==

note over Caller
    JwtAuthenticationToken present in
    SecurityContextHolder (user request)
end note

Caller -> RS : REST request\nAuthorization: Bearer <user JWT>\n(token relayed as-is)
RS -> RS : Same validation + audit\n(user ID / username from JWT claims)
RS --> Caller : 200 OK

legend right
    lakehouse.security.enabled = true/false : master switch
    CSRF disabled (stateless services)
    Secrets via env vars only
end legend
@enduml
